    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0142" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/52<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >1/16</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-04T17:00:00-06:00">June 4, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. Referring to Department’s telegrams of June 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d163-f1"/> and 5 p.m.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d163-f2"/> 1940, I have
                    conferred with President of Honduras<anchor n="81" xml:id="d163-f3"/> who
                    heartily approves proposal and pledges fullest cooperation of Honduran
                    Government. In order to safeguard secrecy his present plan is to limit his
                    representation to two persons namely his Secretary of War, Navy and Aviation,
                    Juan Galvez and his Minister for Foreign Affairs, Salvador Aguirre.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="79" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 29, <ref target="#pg16">p. 16</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="80" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram of June 3, 5 p.m., not found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f3" n="81" xml:id="d163-f3-content">
                <p>Tiburcio Carías Andino.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
